511	We abbreviate ``conditionally linear'' as \emph{CL}. Operationally, an $\ell$-level CL function first applies $L_1$ to $x^{V_1}$; conditioned on the value $x^{L_1}$ it selects a register subspace $V_2$ and a linear map $L_2$ and applies $L_2$ to $x^{V_2}$; and so on, finally outputting $\sum_{k=1}^{\ell} x^{L_k}$. Every $1$-level CL function is linear, and conversely every linear map on $V$ is a $1$-level CL function. Moreover, for every $\ell \ge 1$ the collection of $\ell$-level CL functions contains the collection of $(\ell-1)$-level CL functions.
